+# Recipe candidates cannot prepare pinned derived images through Anvil
+
+**Status:** Fixed locally; pending release
+
+## Problem
+
+`models recipes load` can reproduce a candidate only after its runtime image
+already exists. A model recipe that depends on a revision-pinned Dockerfile or
+small upstream patch therefore required an out-of-band `docker build`, leaving
+the build context, prior tag, provenance, confirmation, and rollback outside the
+Anvil operation contract.
+
+## Resolution
+
+Add `models recipes build-image MODEL --registry REGISTRY` with the normal
+`--dry-run` and `--confirm` gate. A recipe-owned `[recipe.image_build]` table
+selects a relative context and Dockerfile below the operator registry. The
+command hashes the complete context, Dockerfile, and normalized recipe; previews
+the exact build and previous image identity; rejects drift after confirmation;
+and verifies provenance labels on the resulting image. It never loads a model,
+changes a route, or deletes the prior image.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Absolute, escaping, linked, missing, and empty build contexts fail closed.
+- Unknown build fields, invalid booleans/platforms, and non-tag image targets fail.
+- Preview is non-mutating and includes exact digests plus rollback guidance.
+- Apply requires confirmation, rejects input drift, and verifies the built image.
+- The command is declared in the shared CLI/controller command catalog and docs.
+- Hermetic tests cover planning, source validation, successful verification, and
+  provenance mismatch.
